  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "106",
  "quote": "A landlord shall apply a rent deposit that a tenant has paid to the landlord or to a former landlord in payment of the rent for the last rent period before the tenancy terminates.",
  "reason": "Subsection 106(10) requires the landlord to apply a rent deposit solely toward the rent for the last rent period before the tenancy terminates. Because the clause attempts to apply the rent deposit to utility bills and cleaning costs instead, it is inconsistent with the Act and void under section 4."
}

